Overlay patch 0024: truthful Internal Resolution display on iOS/visionOS.
The slider's only consumer (SetResolutionMultiplier -> Fast3dGui's ImGui
game-window viewport) never runs on iOS/visionOS — these builds always
render at the native drawable (iPhone A/B verified identical pixels at
100%/200%; Vision Pro log-verified 3840x2160). A slider stuck at "100%"
reads as half-res to anyone who knows desktop SoH (user flagged it twice),
and persisting 2.0 is a landmine: the multiplier scales POINTS, so if a
future pin ever activates the consumer it would SHRINK the render. Replace
the dead slider with a static truth line on __IOS__ (covers visionOS —
same define, overlay 0022).

--- a/soh/soh/SohGui/SohMenuSettings.cpp
+++ b/soh/soh/SohGui/SohMenuSettings.cpp
@@ -336,6 +336,7 @@
         .RaceDisable(false)
         .Callback([](WidgetInfo& info) { Ship::Context::GetRawInstance()->GetWindow()->ToggleFullscreen(); })
         .Options(ButtonOptions().Tooltip("Toggles Fullscreen On/Off."));
+#ifndef __IOS__
     AddWidget(path, "Internal Resolution", WIDGET_CVAR_SLIDER_FLOAT)
         .CVar(CVAR_INTERNAL_RESOLUTION)
         .RaceDisable(false)
@@ -360,6 +361,17 @@
                 .IsPercentage()
                 .Min(0.5f)
                 .Max(2.0f));
+#else
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0024 rev2): the desktop multiplier stays hidden on
+    // iOS/visionOS. Rev2 (Ghostship SSAA finding, overlay 0036): the render
+    // was in fact SUB-native here — resolution is now governed by the
+    // native-pixel-relative "Supersampling (SSAA)" slider in Settings > iOS
+    // (1.0 = true native). Point there instead of the old (wrong) "always
+    // native" claim.
+    // ASCII only in widget strings (menu font renders em-dash as '?').
+    AddWidget(path, "Internal Resolution: see Supersampling (SSAA) in Settings > iOS (1.0 = native)",
+              WIDGET_SEPARATOR_TEXT);
+#endif
 #ifndef __WIIU__
     AddWidget(path, "Anti-aliasing (MSAA)", WIDGET_CVAR_SLIDER_INT)
         .CVar(CVAR_MSAA_VALUE)
